<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rdf:RDF xml:lang="en" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:org="http://www.w3.org/ns/org#" xmlns:sd="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#" xmlns:sdoe="https://nfdi4culture.de/ontology/schema-extension#">

  <!-- ===== org-extension.xml ===== -->
<!--
           W3C Organization Ontology Terms for the NFDI4Culture Application Profile
           RDFS Implementation, Version 0.1

           This document declares, in RDFS, the terms of the W3C Organization Ontology (org:,
           http://www.w3.org/ns/org#) that are used in the NFDI4Culture modelling of the NFDI4Culture
           Knowledge Graph (CKG). They occur on the Organisation model. Its purpose is to let the modelling
           be loaded with the RDFS versions of CTO 3.0.0 and NFDIcore without importing the Organization
           Ontology as a whole. It is a bridging encoding with the least possible commitment.

           Note that this is NOT a definition of the W3C Organization Ontology. Scope notes describe the terms as
           defined there; domains and ranges reflect NFDI4Culture usage only.

           Created by George Bruseker (Takin.solutions), 2 November 2026
           Namespace of the declared terms : http://www.w3.org/ns/org#

           Contents:
           - 1 property

           Encoding Rules:
           1. Only org: terms used in the NFDI4Culture modelling are declared. They keep their org: IRIs. The
              Organization Ontology's own domain (org:Organization) and range (skos:Concept) are not carried over.

           2. No subclass or subproperty relations are asserted, either among these terms or to CTO, NFDIcore
              or schema.org terms.

           3. Domains and ranges describe current usage in the CKG. Domains are the top-level class
              obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), shared by NFDIcore and CTO, so the properties can be used on any
              class. Ranges are the observed value type where uniform, otherwise obo:BFO_0000001.

           4. Scope notes are represented as rdfs:comment elements: "Scope note" summarises the term as defined
              in its source ontology, and "Implementation note" records how and why it is declared as it is.
           -->

  <!--
           PROPERTIES
           This version counts 1 property.
           -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/org#classification">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">classification</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Indicates a classification for an organization within some classification scheme (W3C Organization Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on organisations (209 uses). Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are schema:DefinedTerm nodes, declared in the schema.org extension.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/org" />
  </rdf:Property>

  <!-- ===== sd-extension.xml ===== -->
<!--
           Software Description Ontology Terms for the NFDI4Culture Application Profile
           RDFS Implementation, Version 0.1

           This document declares, in RDFS, the terms of the Software Description Ontology (sd:,
           https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#) that are used in the NFDI4Culture modelling of the NFDI4Culture
           Knowledge Graph (CKG). They occur on the Software model of the research information graph (RIG).
           Its purpose is to let the modelling be loaded with the RDFS versions of CTO 3.0.0 and NFDIcore
           without importing the Software Description Ontology as a whole. It is a bridging encoding with
           the least possible commitment.

           Note that this is NOT a definition of the Software Description Ontology. Scope notes describe the terms as
           defined there; domains and ranges reflect NFDI4Culture usage only.

           Created by George Bruseker (Takin.solutions), 2 November 2026
           Namespace of the declared terms : https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#

           Contents:
           - 2 classes
           - 5 properties

           Encoding Rules:
           1. Only sd: terms used in the NFDI4Culture modelling are declared. They keep their sd: IRIs.

           2. No subclass or subproperty relations are asserted, either among these terms or to CTO, NFDIcore
              or schema.org terms.

           3. Domains and ranges describe current usage in the CKG. Domains are the top-level class
              obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), shared by NFDIcore and CTO, so the properties can be used on any
              class. Ranges are the observed value type where uniform, otherwise obo:BFO_0000001.

           4. Scope notes are represented as rdfs:comment elements: "Scope note" summarises the term as defined
              in its source ontology, and "Implementation note" records how and why it is declared as it is.
           -->

  <!--
           CLASSES
           This version counts 2 classes.
           -->
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#SourceCode">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Source Code</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The source code of a software component (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Declared because it is the value of sd:hasSourceCode on software (61 nodes). Not yet profiled.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#SoftwareVersion">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Software Version</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A specific release of a software component (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Declared because it is the value of sd:hasVersion on software (4 nodes). Not yet profiled.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdfs:Class>

  <!--
           PROPERTIES
           This version counts 5 properties.
           -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#shortDescription">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">short description</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A short description summarising the purpose of the software (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on software (69 of 82). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#hasSourceCode">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has source code</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Links a software component to its source code (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on software (61 of 82). Range sd:SourceCode: all values are SourceCode nodes.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#SourceCode" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#hasDocumentation">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has documentation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Links a software component to its documentation (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on software (15 of 82). All values are xsd:anyURI.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#hasVersion">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has version</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Links a software component to one of its released versions (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on software (3 of 82). Range sd:SoftwareVersion: all values are SoftwareVersion nodes.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#SoftwareVersion" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd#hasInstallationInstructions">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has installation instructions</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Instructions describing how to install the software (Software Description Ontology).

Implementation note:
Used on software (1 of 82). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/okn/o/sd" />
  </rdf:Property>

  <!-- ===== schema-org-extension.xml ===== -->
<!--
           Schema.org Terms for the NFDI4Culture Application Profile
           RDFS Implementation, Version 0.2

           This document declares, in RDFS, the schema.org terms that are used in the NFDI4Culture
           modelling of the NFDI4Culture Knowledge Graph (CKG), both the research
           data graph (RDG) and the research information graph (RIG), and that are not already declared in the
           Culture Ontology (CTO) 3.0.0. Its purpose is to let the modelling be loaded together with the
           RDFS versions of CTO 3.0.0 and NFDIcore without importing schema.org as a whole, whose
           semantics are not compatible with these ontologies. It is a bridging encoding with the least
           possible commitment: it describes how the terms are currently used in the CKG and adds no
           alignment between schema.org and CTO or NFDIcore.

           Note that this is NOT a definition of schema.org. Scope notes are quoted from schema.org;
           domains and ranges reflect NFDI4Culture usage only.

           Created by George Bruseker (Takin.solutions), 2 November 2026
           Version 0.2 (2 November 2026): adds the schema.org terms used in the Data feed,
           Data portal and Research Information Graph (RIG) models
           Namespace of terms introduced here : https://nfdi4culture.de/ontology/schema-extension#

           Contents:
           - 15 classes
           - 40 properties
           - 1 inverse property

           Encoding Rules:
           1. Only schema.org terms used in the NFDI4Culture modelling and not declared in CTO 3.0.0 are
              declared here. schema:associatedMedia, schema:dataFeedElement, schema:item and
              schema:license are declared in CTO 3.0.0 and are not repeated.

           2. schema.org terms keep their schema.org IRIs, in the namespace used by CTO 3.0.0
              (https://schema.org/). No new IRIs are minted except nfdi-schema:CoordinateBearer.

           3. Domains and ranges describe current usage in the CKG and refer to NFDIcore or CTO classes
              where these exist. Where a property is used on several classes, its domain (and, for
              object values, its range) is the top-level class obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), shared by
              NFDIcore and CTO, so the property can be used on any class. Mixed literal values get
              rdfs:Literal; values that are external IRIs get rdfs:Resource. The one exception is
              schema:latitude / schema:longitude, for which nfdi-schema:CoordinateBearer is the domain.

           4. No subclass or subproperty relations are asserted, either among these terms or to CTO and
              NFDIcore terms. schema.org's own schema:domainIncludes and schema:rangeIncludes are not
              carried over.

           5. RDFS cannot express inverse properties. schema:member, the inverse of schema:memberOf in
              schema.org, is declared separately in the section on inverse properties, without an axiom.

           6. Scope notes are represented as rdfs:comment elements: "Scope note" quotes schema.org, and
              "Implementation note" records how and why the term is declared as it is.
           -->

  <!--
           CLASSES
           This version counts 15 classes.
           -->
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/DefinedTerm">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Defined Term</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A word, name, acronym, phrase, etc. with a formal definition. Often used in the context of category or subject classification, glossaries or dictionaries, product or creative work types, etc. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it appears as a value type in the NFDI4Culture modelling. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/Role">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Role</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Represents additional information about a relationship or property. For example a Role can be used to say that a 'member' role linking some SportsTeam to a player occurred during a particular time period. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it appears in the schema:memberOf and schema:member paths in the NFDI4Culture modelling (Person → schema:memberOf → schema:Role → schema:memberOf → Organisation). No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://nfdi4culture.de/ontology/schema-extension#CoordinateBearer">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Coordinate Bearer</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
This class comprises anything that carries schema:latitude and schema:longitude in the NFDI4Culture Knowledge Graph.

Implementation note:
Introduced only to serve as the domain of schema:latitude and schema:longitude, which are used both on cto:CTO_0001005 (source item) and on schema:GeoCoordinates. RDFS cannot express a union; membership of this class follows from use of the two properties. No subclass relations are asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/NewsArticle">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">News Article</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A NewsArticle is an article whose content reports news, or provides background context and supporting materials for understanding the news. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is a model in the RIG weave (273 entities). No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/Event">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Event</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An event happening at a certain time and location, such as a concert, lecture, or festival. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is a model in the RIG weave (152 entities). Distinct from nfdicore:NFDI_0000131 (event) used in the RDG. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/EventSeries">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Event Series</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A series of Events. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is a model in the RIG weave (13 entities). No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/CreateAction">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Create Action</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The act of deliberately creating/producing/generating/building a result out of the agent. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is the value of schema:potentialAction on RIG models. Not yet profiled.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/ConsumeAction">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Consume Action</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The act of ingesting information/resources/food. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is the value of schema:potentialAction on data feeds. Not yet profiled.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/Review">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Review</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A review of an item - for example, of a restaurant, movie, or store. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is the value of schema:review on NFDI resources. Not yet profiled.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/WebApplication">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Web Application</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Web applications. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because RIG entities are typed with it (27 without a main NFDI class). No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/LearningResource">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Learning Resource</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The LearningResource type can be used to indicate CreativeWorks (whether physical or digital) that have a particular and explicit orientation towards learning, education, skill acquisition, and other educational purposes. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because RIG entities are typed with it. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/VideoObject">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Video Object</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A video file. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because RIG media entities are typed with it. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/CreativeWork">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Creative Work</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The most generic kind of creative work, including books, movies, photographs, software programs, etc. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is one of the types carried by the value of cto:CTO_0001025 (related real world entity) on source items. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/VisualArtwork">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Visual Artwork</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
A work of art that is primarily visual in character. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because it is one of the types carried by the value of cto:CTO_0001025 (related real world entity) on source items. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://schema.org/GeoCoordinates">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Geo Coordinates</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The geographic coordinates of a place or event. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Declared because schema:latitude and schema:longitude are used on it in the CKG. No superclass is asserted.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdfs:Class>

  <!--
           PROPERTIES
           This version counts 40 properties.
           Properties are grouped by the NFDI4Culture model in which they are used.
           -->

  <!-- Person (nfdicore:NFDI_0000004) -->
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/familyName">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">family name</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Family name. In the U.S., the last name of a Person. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Used only on nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/givenName">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">given name</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Given name. In the U.S., the first name of a Person. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Used only on nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/additionalName">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">additional name</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An additional name for a Person, can be used for a middle name. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Used only on nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/honorificPrefix">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">honorific prefix</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An honorific prefix preceding a Person's name such as Dr/Mrs/Mr. (schema.org)

Examples:
- "Prof. Dr."

Implementation note:
Used only on nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/honorificSuffix">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">honorific suffix</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An honorific suffix following a Person's name such as M.D./PhD/MSCSW. (schema.org)

Examples:
- "M.A."

Implementation note:
Used only on nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). All values are xsd:string.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/knows">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knows</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
The most generic bi-directional social/work relation. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Used between instances of nfdicore:NFDI_0000004 (person). One occurrence in the CKG.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0000004" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/knowsAbout">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knows about</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
Of a Person, and less typically of an Organization, to indicate a topic that is known about - suggesting possible expertise but not implying it. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: used on person and project. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are typed schema:DefinedTerm, nfdicore:NFDI_0000100 (academic discipline) and nfdicore:NFDI_0000206 (standard). Deliberately not a subproperty of nfdicore:NFDI_0000211 (has subject area), which would infer every value to be an academic discipline.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001" />
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://schema.org/" />
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://schema.org/memberOf">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">member of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Scope note:
An Organization (or ProgramMembership) to which this Person or Organization belongs. (schema.org)

Implementation note:
Domain obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: subjects are person and schema:Role. Range obo:BFO_0000001 (entity), the top-level class: values are schema:Role, organisation, NFDI consortium and project. In the NFDI4Culture data the property is used twice in the path Person → schema:memberOf → schema:Role → schema:memberOf → Organisation.
</rdfs:comment>
